  "body": "What changed\n\n- New `crates/ui/src/egui_app/frame_rate.rs`: the frame-rate reading and its log rule. It reads the frame stamps that the shell already takes (frame cost rule, #2238). Work for each frame is O(1). It never requests a repaint.\n- Log rule: a new level (15 percent and at least 5 fps) logs one line. A rate that keeps moving logs one summary (min, max, mean) at most each 10 s. An idle application logs nothing (a gap over 250 ms restarts the reading).\n- `gpu: slow frame` now uses the same 10 s limit (was 5 s).\n- The Debug info panel is a dock tab (`Tab::DebugInfo`). The status strip door toggles it with `LayoutRequest::ToggleDebugInfo`. It can be dragged out to a float and back. Its own X closes it. The report shows a `Frame rate:` line.\n- Layout is view state, not a command. The dock is not saved today, so this PR does not add dock persistence (see the decision file).\n\nOverlap: the frame-cost stack (#2254, #2255, #2259, #2264, #2266) was checked. Only `state.rs` is shared and the lines differ. This PR is based on main and is not stacked.\n\nTests (pinning)\n\n- `egui_app::frame_rate::tests::one_level_change_logs_one_line_and_noise_logs_none`\n- `egui_app::frame_rate::tests::a_rate_that_keeps_moving_logs_once_each_10_s_with_min_max_mean`\n- `egui_app::frame_rate::tests::an_idle_application_logs_nothing_and_reads_idle`\n- `egui_app::tests::layout::the_debug_info_panel_is_present_docked_and_undocked`\n- `egui_app::frame_watch::tests::reports_are_rate_limited_but_counted`\n- `egui_app::debug_info_tests::the_report_gives_the_frame_rate_or_says_idle`\n\nRun: those tests, the `structural` and `layout` filters (28 pass), and clippy `-p camcraft-ui --all-targets -D warnings`.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nHeadless render of the real shell (test harness, 1280x720). Before is `origin/main`. After is the PR head.\n\nBefore: the Debug info panel is a floating window over the browser pane.\n\n![before floating](<https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/screenshots/pr-2278/before-floating.png>)\n\nAfter: the panel is docked as a tab beside the properties pane. The report has the new `Frame rate:` line.\n\n![after docked](<https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/screenshots/pr-2278/after-docked.png>)\n\nAfter, dragged out: the panel is a floating window with its own tab title.\n\n![after floating](<https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/screenshots/pr-2278/after-floating.png>)\n\nNot exercised\n\n- The windowed app was not started. The screenshots come from the headless test harness render of the real shell.\n- The full ui suites and the wasm shell were not run. The wasm shell does not feed the frame-rate reading.\n- The old floating-window tests (fold, close button) were removed. The dock owns the title row now.\n\nChangelog: Debug info logs the frame rate when it changes (at most once each 10 s) and is a dockable panel.\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #2262\n\n",
